 in a Raffle contract that cannot transfer, redeem, or refund it"],"explanation":"Raffle._update (line 498) screens ticket recipients via _isProtocolDestination(to, address(prizeToken)) to enforce the invariant that protocol contracts cannot own tickets and strand claims. However, _isProtocolDestination (lines 602-604) only queries canonicalFactory.isRaffle(to) when to.code.length != 0, and OpenZeppelin ERC721._safeMint skips onERC721Received when to.code.length == 0. Because RaffleFactory deploys clones at deterministic CREATE addresses via Clones.clone, a buyer can pass a not-yet-deployed Raffle clone address as recipient in buyEntries. Once that sibling Raffle clone is deployed by a subsequent createRaffle call, the ticket is owned by a Raffle clone (isRaffle[recipient] == true), which has no mechanism to transfer, redeem, or refund the ticket (and _transferQuote also rejects isRaffle addresses), permanently locking the prize or refund liability.","dedupe_is_canonical":true,"dedupe_canonical_id":3,"dedupe_cluster_id":"1:3"}]

